\subsection{Review Decision}

A [[ReviewDecision]] captures the review state of a single paper, including
its status and associated tags.

It also remembers which searches returned the paper ([[found_by]]).
A session accumulates many searches, often several on one provider, and
the [[provider]] field alone cannot tell them apart.  [[prov found-via]]
used to fill that gap by picking one search for the provider, and so
named a query that had never returned the paper
(\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholar/issues/128}).  Only the moment a
result is turned into decisions knows which search a paper came from,
so that is where the link is recorded (\cref{sec:review-found-by}).  A
link is the [[(query, provider, filters)]] key of the search's
[[SearchRecord]], the key that identifies a record in the session
(\cref{sec:search-record-key}), so it always resolves to the stored
query, filters and limit.  Its third part is the [[filters_key]] of the
record's filters, the empty string for an unfiltered search.  Links
saved before filters were part of the key have only the query and the
provider; they load with [[None]] in the third part unless the session
holds exactly one record with that query and provider
(\cref{sec:session-persistence}).  The list stays empty when
nothing was recorded: decisions saved before the link existed, and
papers added by snowballing, which no search returned.

An old link without filters says only that \emph{some} search of its
query and provider returned the paper (\cref{sec:session-persistence}).
Once the paper also has a resolved link for that query and provider, the
old one adds nothing a reader can use: found-via would print the
resolved command and, beside it, a \enquote{not reproducible} note about
the same query.  So a resolved link supersedes the unresolved links of
its query and provider ([[without_superseded_links]]), whenever a link
is recorded and when a file is read.

<<review data structures>>=
def without_superseded_links(
    links: list[tuple[str, str, str | None]],
) -> list[tuple[str, str, str | None]]:
    """Drop each unresolved link whose query and provider have a resolved one."""
    resolved = {(q, p) for q, p, key in links if key is not None}
    return [
        link for link in links
        if link[2] is not None or link[:2] not in resolved
    ]


@dataclass
class ReviewDecision:
    """
    A review decision for a single paper.

    Tracks whether the paper was kept or discarded during review,
    along with tags (themes for kept, motivations for discarded).

    Attributes:
        paper: The Paper being reviewed.
        provider: Which search provider returned this paper.
        status: Current decision status (pending/kept/discarded).
        tags: List of tags (themes for kept, motivations for discarded).
        source: Where the decision came from (human or LLM).
        is_example: True if this paper is a training example for LLM.
        llm_confidence: Confidence score from LLM (0.0-1.0), if applicable.
        llm_model, llm_decided_at, llm_prompt_version, llm_reason,
            llm_abstract_truncated: what `scholar llm classify` recorded
            about its decision (see `LLM_AUDIT_FIELDS`); `None` when
            unknown, as for decisions made before they were recorded.
        found_by: The `(query, provider, filters key)` keys of the search
            records whose results contained the paper, in the order
            recorded; empty when not recorded (sessions saved before the
            link existed, snowballing). The filters key is `None` for an
            old link that could not be tied to one record.
        same_id_copies: Other works a search returned under this
            paper's DOI-less id, with years too far apart to be the same
            work (`{"year", "venue", "provider"}` each); see
            `is_same_id_namesake`.
    """
    paper: Paper
    provider: str
    status: DecisionStatus = DecisionStatus.PENDING
    tags: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)
    source: ReviewSource = ReviewSource.HUMAN
    is_example: bool = False
    llm_confidence: float | None = None
    <<LLM audit fields of a decision>>
    found_by: list[tuple[str, str, str | None]] = field(default_factory=list)
    same_id_copies: list[dict] = field(default_factory=list)

    def __post_init__(self):
        """Coerce None list fields to empty lists."""
        if self.tags is None:
            self.tags = []
        if self.found_by is None:
            self.found_by = []
        if self.same_id_copies is None:
            self.same_id_copies = []

    def add_same_id_copy(self, copy: dict) -> None:
        """Note another work returned under this paper's id, once."""
        if copy not in self.same_id_copies:
            self.same_id_copies.append(copy)

    def note_same_id_copy(self, paper: Paper, provider: str) -> None:
        """Note `paper` as another work returned under this paper's id."""
        self.add_same_id_copy(
            {"year": paper.year, "venue": paper.venue, "provider": provider}
        )

    def record_search(
        self, query: str, provider: str, key: str | None
    ) -> None:
        """Note that the search `(query, provider, key)` returned this paper.

        `key` is the `filters_key` of the search's filters, or `None` for
        an old link that names no filters.
        """
        if (query, provider, key) not in self.found_by:
            self.found_by = without_superseded_links(
                self.found_by + [(query, provider, key)]
            )

    @property
    def is_decided(self) -> bool:
        """Check if a decision has been made."""
        return self.status != DecisionStatus.PENDING
    
    @property
    def is_valid(self) -> bool:
        """
        Check if the decision is valid.
        
        Discarded papers require at least one tag (motivation).
        Kept and pending papers are always valid.
        """
        if self.status == DecisionStatus.DISCARDED:
            return len(self.tags) > 0
        return True
    
    def add_tag(self, tag: str) -> None:
        """Add a tag if not already present."""
        if tag and tag not in self.tags:
            self.tags.append(tag)
    
    def remove_tag(self, tag: str) -> None:
        """Remove a tag if present."""
        if tag in self.tags:
            self.tags.remove(tag)
    
    def has_tag(self, tag: str) -> bool:
        """Check if this decision has a specific tag."""
        return tag in self.tags
    
    def clear_tags(self) -> None:
        """Remove all tags."""
        self.tags.clear()
    
    # Backward compatibility for code using 'motivation' as single string
    @property
    def motivation(self) -> str:
        """Get first tag as motivation (backward compatibility)."""
        return self.tags[0] if self.tags else ""
    
    @motivation.setter
    def motivation(self, value: str) -> None:
        """Set motivation as single tag (backward compatibility)."""
        self.tags = [value] if value else []
@

