\label{sec:superseded-merged}
A merged record cannot be split, but it can be superseded.  When the
user re-runs its query with the current code, the new run records one
search per provider, and those records stood beside the old merged one
(a copy of a real session went from 4 to 6 records for one re-run):
the caption's \enquote{for k of n queries} and the report then counted
that query twice for each of its providers.  Once there is a record of
the same query and filters for \emph{every} provider the merged record
names ([[merged_record_cover]]), the merged record says nothing those
records do not, except a count that could never be attributed, so it is
dropped ([[supersede_merged_records]]).  A merged record that only some
providers have re-run stays: dropping it would lose the only record of
the others.

A record covers only if it can stand in for the provider's part of the
merged search.  It must have answered: a skipped search or an HTTP~500
says nothing about what the provider holds, and dropping the merged
record for it would turn an answered search into a failed one.  And it
must have asked for at least as much: a re-run with [[-l 5]] cannot
stand in for a merged search with [[-l 100]], whose papers it may not
include.  A merged record whose limit is unknown (the merge of two
different limits stores none) is covered by any answered record, since
nothing is known to compare with.  Without these two conditions a plain
load and save of real sessions dropped merged records that no answered
search covered; with them, a merged record is dropped only where it
really counted a search twice.

The papers linked to the merged record keep a link to the search, now
per provider.  A paper that the new run returned already has links to
the records of the providers that returned it ([[found_in]],
\cref{sec:review-found-by}), which is more precise than the old link,
so the old link is simply dropped.  A paper that the new run did not
return is linked to the records of all the merged providers, which is
what the old link said: one of them returned it.

The positions of the query parts and the providers correspond, since
the merge joined both in the same order ([[q1 | q2]] with
[[openalex, dblp]]); a query whose parts are all equal, the usual case,
covers every provider.  The rule runs wherever records come together:
at the end of [[create_review_session]], and at the end of a save's
merge with the file (\cref{sec:session-integrity}), since another
process may have re-run the query, or may still hold the merged record
this process dropped.

<<review session functions>>=
def merged_record_cover(
    record: SearchRecord, records: list[SearchRecord]
) -> list[SearchRecord] | None:
    """The per-provider records that supersede a merged `record`, or None.

    One record of the same query and filters is needed for each
    provider the merged record names, one that answered and asked for
    at least the merged record's limit (any limit when that is
    unknown); None if any is missing.
    """
    if not record.is_merged:
        return None
    providers = record.merged_providers
    queries = record.query.split(" | ")
    if len(queries) != len(providers):
        if len(set(queries)) != 1:
            return None
        queries = queries[:1] * len(providers)
    key = filters_key(record.filters)

    def wide_enough(other: SearchRecord) -> bool:
        if record.limit is None:
            return True
        return other.limit is not None and (
            search_width(other.limit) >= search_width(record.limit)
        )

    cover = []
    for provider, query in zip(providers, queries):
        match = next((
            r for r in records
            if not r.is_merged and r.provider == provider
            and r.query == query and filters_key(r.filters) == key
            and not failed_outright(r) and wide_enough(r)
        ), None)
        if match is None:
            return None
        cover.append(match)
    return cover


def supersede_merged_records(session: "ReviewSession") -> None:
    """Drop each merged record that per-provider records fully cover.

    Links to it are dropped where the paper links to a covering record
    already, and otherwise replaced by links to all covering records.
    """
    for record in list(session.search_records):
        cover = merged_record_cover(record, session.search_records)
        if cover is None:
            continue
        session.search_records.remove(record)
        cover_keys = [r.key for r in cover]
        for decision in session.decisions:
            old = [
                link for link in decision.found_by
                if link[:2] == (record.query, record.provider)
                and link[2] in (None, record.key[2])
            ]
            if not old:
                continue
            links = [link for link in decision.found_by if link not in old]
            if not any(link in cover_keys for link in links):
                links += cover_keys
            decision.found_by = without_superseded_links(
                list(dict.fromkeys(links))
            )
