The same order must hold when a save meets the other process's record
of the same search (\cref{sec:session-integrity}).  The reviewer's
case: the session is at [[-l 5]]; process~B re-runs with [[-l 0]] and
saves fifty hits; process~A, still holding the [[-l 5]] record, saves
a decision.  The file must keep B's wide record with its dates.  And the
mirror: A holds the wide re-run when B saves its narrow copy, and A's
wide record must survive A's save.

