A partial re-run is not a failed one.  The case found in the review of
the S2 bulk search: an old relevance answer of 0 for [[a AND b]], then
a newer bulk re-run with five papers, cut short.  The record must show
the five, marked incomplete.  A newer partial re-run with fewer papers
than the earlier answer replaces it too, since it is the latest search,
and the papers of the earlier run stay; only between undated records
does the count decide; and a wider earlier answer still wins over a
narrower partial one.

