Filters are part of a search's key (\cref{sec:search-record-key}).
Let's verify it with the two runs of
\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholar/issues/140}: one query on one
provider, once per year range, appended to one session.  Both records
must survive with their own filters and hits, each paper must link to
the run that returned it, and the failed re-run rule must still apply
within one filter set---and only there: a failed run with new filters
is a failed search, which an answer of other filters cannot stand in
for.  Everything goes through the real
[[create_review_session]], [[save_session]] and [[load_session]].

