Papers from the previous session that do not appear in the current search
results must still be included---the user has already reviewed them. We copy
them directly from the previous session to preserve all metadata.

A session without a session file has its decisions only in the old
per-query store of the notes module, whose records
([[ReviewDecisionRecord]], \cref{notes-module}) keep beside each
decision the paper details needed to rebuild it: title, authors, year,
DOI, abstract, venue, URL, PDF link and the provider that found it.
Two places rebuild a paper from such a record: the restore below, for
papers the re-run did not return, and the conversion of the search
results (\cref{sec:decision-store-fallback}), for papers it did.  Both
build it with [[paper_from_decision_record]], so a paper the re-run
returns again starts from the same stored paper as one it does not.
The record's provider is the paper's only known source; a record
without one gets the placeholder [[previous]], as it always did (every
record in the user's ten decision files names its provider, so the
placeholder is a guard, not a common case).

<<review session functions>>=
def paper_from_decision_record(record: Any) -> Paper:
    """The paper stored in a record of the old per-query decision store.

    `record` is a `notes.ReviewDecisionRecord`.  Derived identifiers
    (an arXiv DOI) are filled in, as for a paper loaded from a session.
    """
    paper = Paper(
        title=record.title,
        authors=record.authors if record.authors else [],
        year=record.year,
        doi=record.doi,
        abstract=record.abstract,
        venue=record.venue,
        url=record.url,
        pdf_url=record.pdf_url,
        sources=[getattr(record, "provider", None) or "previous"],
    )
    return _normalize_paper_identifiers(paper)
@

<<restore papers not in current results>>=
if prev_decision_lookup:
    # Use session data (preserves all fields)
    for paper_id, prev_dec in prev_decision_lookup.items():
        if paper_id not in current_paper_ids:
            session.decisions.append(prev_dec)
elif previous_decisions:
    # Fallback to notes module (older format, no LLM fields)
    for paper_id, prev in previous_decisions.decisions.items():
        if paper_id not in current_paper_ids:
            paper = paper_from_decision_record(prev)
            status = DecisionStatus.PENDING
            if prev.status == "kept":
                status = DecisionStatus.KEPT
            elif prev.status == "discarded":
                status = DecisionStatus.DISCARDED
            
            tags = extract_tags_from_record(prev)
            
            # Restore LLM fields from notes if available
            source = ReviewSource.HUMAN
            source_str = getattr(prev, 'source', 'human')
            try:
                source = ReviewSource(source_str)
            except ValueError:
                pass
            
            session.decisions.append(
                ReviewDecision(
                    paper=paper,
                    provider=getattr(prev, 'provider', "previous"),
                    status=status,
                    tags=tags,
                    source=source,
                    is_example=getattr(prev, 'is_example', False),
                    llm_confidence=getattr(prev, 'llm_confidence', None),
                )
            )
