The case comes from the real session: an abstract and enrichment from
OpenAlex, then a Semantic Scholar bulk copy without them.  Each run gets
its own paper registry, as two command-line runs would: in one process
the registry hands [[Paper.from_dict]] the object already held, which
hid the loss from a test that saved and reloaded in one registry.  The
DOI-less stored entry stays beside the new DOI copy, as every append
leaves such copies for [[sessions reconcile]] (\cref{sec:session-copies}).

