\paragraph{One work under two ids.}
The opposite case is more common: one provider records a paper with
its DOI and another without, and the two copies get two ids and two
decisions.  In the integrity review that raised issue~\#170 this was
3.5\,\% of the records, and the copies of 258 works had been given
different decisions.  Each DOI-less decision is paired with its DOI
copy by [[doi_copy_of]], the search-time rule, and what may be done
with a pair depends on what the two decisions say:
\begin{description}
\item[Foldable] One is pending and carries no tags and no trace of a
  machine: nobody has screened it, so it can be folded into the
  decided one, which keeps its decision, tags and source.  A pending
  decision with a machine source or LLM audit fields
  ([[LLM_AUDIT_FIELDS]]) is a classifier's withheld answer, not an
  unscreened record, and is kept.  Two equal decisions can be folded
  too, and lose nothing by becoming one: [[decision_state]] compares the
  source and the audit fields as well, so an unreviewed machine
  decision is never \enquote{equal} to a human one, and no fold changes
  a decision's source.  A DOI-less copy without a year or an author is
  never folded ([[foldable_copy]], \cref{sec:doi-less-copies} in the
  scholar module): on the title alone, a DOI-less
  \enquote{Introduction} is anybody's introduction.
\item[Both are decided] but differ in status, tags or source: which
  decision stands, or how to merge two sets of tags, is a judgement the
  session does not make.  Both stay, and are listed for the user
  (below).
\end{description}

\paragraph{Folding is a command, not a side effect.}
A first version folded the copies at the end of every append, in
memory, and saved the result whenever the session was next saved---after
a whole TUI session with [[--review]].  Every way of making that safe
failed against another process in the meantime: two processes making
the same fold undid each other, a note read in the TUI moved to the DOI
id ([[get_note]] migrates a legacy hash id on read) before a fold that
was later undone, an undo threw away enrichment done to the survivor
after the fold, and a process that had loaded the session before a fold
brought the folded copy back, because the merge with the file knows
additions but not deletions.  An append therefore never folds; it only
lists (below).  Folding is [[scholar sessions reconcile]], which
[[reconcile_session]] implements: it takes the session's file lock,
loads the file fresh, folds, writes, and only after the write moves the
notes, to the ids the folded entries have at that moment.  The lock is
held for the milliseconds this takes, so no other process can save in
between, and nothing needs to be undone.  The lock is the one
[[save_session]] takes; it is reentrant within a process, so the save
inside the reconcile takes it again without waiting for itself.

The folded entry takes the DOI copy's paper, filled from the DOI-less
copy without overwriting anything ([[merge_version_of]]), so its id is
the DOI.  The search links, the other-work notes and the provider names
of both copies are united (the names joined by a comma, as a session
records a paper several providers returned, \cref{sec:review-found-by}), so provenance points at every search that
returned either copy.  A pair whose copies both carry a note is not
folded, because [[migrate_paper_id]] keeps the target's note and drops
the moved one when both ids have a note.  If the notes file cannot be
read, nothing is folded.

<<review session functions>>=
def united_providers(*providers: str | None) -> str:
    """Join the provider names of several decisions, each name once."""
    names = [
        name.strip()
        for provider in providers
        for name in re.split(r"[;,|]", provider or "")
        if name.strip()
    ]
    return ", ".join(dict.fromkeys(names))


def _fold_direction(
    bare: ReviewDecision, with_doi: ReviewDecision
) -> tuple[ReviewDecision, ReviewDecision] | None:
    """Return (survivor, absorbed) for a copy pair, or None to keep both."""
    if decision_state(bare) == decision_state(with_doi):
        return with_doi, bare
    if is_unscreened(bare):
        return with_doi, bare
    if is_unscreened(with_doi):
        return bare, with_doi
    return None


def is_unscreened(decision: ReviewDecision) -> bool:
    """Whether nobody, human or machine, has looked at `decision`."""
    return (
        decision.status == DecisionStatus.PENDING and not decision.tags
        and decision.source == ReviewSource.HUMAN
        and decision.llm_confidence is None
        and not any(llm_audit_of(decision).values())
    )


def _doi_copy_pairs(
    session: ReviewSession,
) -> list[tuple[ReviewDecision, ReviewDecision]]:
    """Pair each DOI-less decision with the decision of its DOI copy."""
    papers = [d.paper for d in session.decisions]
    index = doi_copy_index(papers)
    pairs = []
    for decision in session.decisions:
        target = doi_copy_of(decision.paper, papers, index)
        if target is not None:
            pairs.append((decision, session.decisions[target]))
    return pairs


def foldable_copies(
    session: ReviewSession,
) -> list[tuple[ReviewDecision, ReviewDecision]]:
    """The copy pairs `reconcile_copies` would fold (notes aside)."""
    return [
        (bare, with_doi) for bare, with_doi in _doi_copy_pairs(session)
        if foldable_copy(bare.paper)
        and _fold_direction(bare, with_doi) is not None
    ]


def reconcile_copies(session: ReviewSession) -> list[tuple[str, str]]:
    """Fold the foldable copy pairs of `session`, in memory.

    Each fold is recorded in `session.folded` (old id to new id). Notes
    are not moved; `reconcile_session` does that after the write.
    Returns the `(old id, new id)` of each fold.
    """
    pairs = foldable_copies(session)
    if not pairs:
        return []
    try:
        noted = {note.paper_id for note in list_papers_with_notes()}
    except NotesFileError as error:
        logger.warning("%s; copies of one work were not folded", error)
        return []
    folds: list[tuple[str, str]] = []
    removed: set[int] = set()
    for bare, with_doi in pairs:
        if {id(bare), id(with_doi)} & removed:
            continue
        bare_id, doi_id = get_paper_id(bare.paper), get_paper_id(with_doi.paper)
        if bare_id in noted and doi_id in noted:
            continue
        survivor, absorbed = _fold_direction(bare, with_doi)
        <<fold [[absorbed]] into [[survivor]]>>
        session.folded[bare_id] = doi_id
        folds.append((bare_id, doi_id))
        if bare_id in noted:
            noted.add(doi_id)
        removed.add(id(absorbed))
    session.decisions = [d for d in session.decisions if id(d) not in removed]
    repoint_folded_ids(session)
    session._invalidate_cache()
    return folds
