\paragraph{What is left for the user.}
What is not folded is listed, never silently kept.  Four kinds remain,
all found by reading the session only, so [[sessions show]] and the
report can list them for any session, old ones included, without
changing it:
\begin{description}
\item[Foldable copies] ([[foldable_copies]]): pairs that
  [[sessions reconcile]] would fold.  They are counted with a hint to
  run it.
\item[Conflicting copies] ([[conflicting_copies]]): a pair decided with
  different statuses, and a decision under whose DOI-less id a search
  also returned a work of a distant year.
\item[Copies decided alike, not merged] ([[alike_copies]]): a pair with
  the same status but different tags or sources.  Folding them would
  mean choosing tags or a source for the user.
\item[Possible copies, not reconciled] ([[possible_copies]]): DOI-less
  decisions that the audit table would merge with a DOI decision
  ([[audit_work_key]]) but that are in none of the lists above.  The
  pairing uses the exact title-and-surname hash, while the audit
  table's key ignores punctuation, case and year, so it joins more: on
  copies of the real sessions behind issue~\#170, the review of this
  change found 2\,995 DOI-less records that share a work key with a DOI
  record, of which only 403 were pairs.  The rest, and the pairs that
  cannot be folded (no year or author, a pending copy with tags or a
  machine's trace), are counted here, so that nothing goes
  unreconciled without being said.  Folding is not widened to that key:
  it ignores the year, and a fold is not taken back.
\end{description}
[[copy_conflict_line]] says in one line what the user needs to decide:
the two copies' ids, decisions (with the source when it is not a
human), providers and tags, or the two years (and venues, when they
differ) of works that share an id.

<<review session functions>>=
@dataclass
class CopyConflict:
    """Copies of one work decided differently, or two works under one id.

    `decisions` holds the session's copies (two for a DOI and a DOI-less
    copy, one for an id shared by several works); `copies` the other
    works a search returned under that id.
    """

    decisions: list[ReviewDecision]
    copies: list[dict] = field(default_factory=list)


def _decided_pairs(
    session: ReviewSession,
) -> list[tuple[ReviewDecision, ReviewDecision]]:
    """The copy pairs that could be folded, both decided, not equal."""
    return [
        (bare, with_doi) for bare, with_doi in _doi_copy_pairs(session)
        if foldable_copy(bare.paper)
        and bare.is_decided and with_doi.is_decided
        and decision_state(bare) != decision_state(with_doi)
    ]


def conflicting_copies(session: ReviewSession) -> list[CopyConflict]:
    """List the copy conflicts in `session` that a user must resolve."""
    conflicts = [
        CopyConflict([bare, with_doi])
        for bare, with_doi in _decided_pairs(session)
        if bare.status != with_doi.status
    ]
    conflicts += [
        CopyConflict([d], list(d.same_id_copies))
        for d in session.decisions if d.same_id_copies
    ]
    return conflicts


def alike_copies(session: ReviewSession) -> list[CopyConflict]:
    """List the copy pairs decided with one status but not merged."""
    return [
        CopyConflict([bare, with_doi])
        for bare, with_doi in _decided_pairs(session)
        if bare.status == with_doi.status
    ]


def possible_copies(session: ReviewSession) -> list[ReviewDecision]:
    """List DOI-less decisions sharing a work key with a DOI decision.

    Those in a foldable, conflicting or alike pair are left out: they
    are listed there.
    """
    listed = {id(bare) for bare, _ in _decided_pairs(session)}
    listed |= {id(bare) for bare, _ in foldable_copies(session)}
    doi_keys = {
        audit_work_key(d.paper) for d in session.decisions if d.paper.doi
    }
    return [
        d for d in session.decisions
        if not d.paper.doi and id(d) not in listed
        and audit_work_key(d.paper)[0]
        and audit_work_key(d.paper) in doi_keys
    ]


def copy_conflict_line(conflict: CopyConflict) -> str:
    """Describe one copy conflict in a line of plain text."""
    first = conflict.decisions[0]
    title = first.paper.title or "(untitled)"
    if not conflict.copies:
        def copy(d: ReviewDecision) -> str:
            tags = f" [{', '.join(d.tags)}]" if d.tags else ""
            by = ("" if d.source == ReviewSource.HUMAN
                  else f" by {d.source.value}")
            return (f"{get_paper_id(d.paper)} {d.status.value}{by} "
                    f"({d.provider}){tags}")
        return f"{title}: " + ", ".join(copy(d) for d in conflict.decisions)

    def when(year, venue, shown_venue):
        text = str(year) if year else "no year"
        return f"{text}, {venue}" if venue and shown_venue else text

    held = first.paper
    others = "; ".join(
        when(c.get("year"), c.get("venue"), c.get("venue") != held.venue)
        + f" ({c.get('provider')})"
        for c in conflict.copies
    )
    venue_differs = any(c.get("venue") != held.venue for c in conflict.copies)
    return (
        f"{title} ({get_paper_id(held)}): {first.status.value} as "
        f"{when(held.year, held.venue, venue_differs)}; also returned as "
        f"{others}; probably different works sharing one id"
    )
