The tests go through the real [[create_review_session]],
[[reconcile_session]], save and load, with the notes and session files
in the test's own data directory.  First the namesakes: an editorial of
2018, kept, and one of 2023 under the same id; then the copies: a DBLP
record without a DOI and the OpenAlex record with it.  Most races are
played out in one process with two session objects, one loaded before
the other's save, which is what a second process amounts to for the
merge; the race that the re-review found with real processes (a stale
process against a fresh decision on the DOI copy) is run in real
subprocesses, so that it tests the files and the lock, not the paper
registry that one process shares between its session objects.

