\paragraph{A warning when a save still drops decisions.}
The merge covers every session that was loaded, but not a session object
built without a baseline and saved over an existing file, nor a bug in a
future command.  As a last line of defence [[save_session]] compares the
number of decided (non-pending) papers on disk with the number it is about
to write.  A drop is legitimate only when this process itself reset
decisions to pending (the TUI can undo a decision), and those resets are
exactly the decisions whose baseline was decided and whose state is now
pending.  The other legitimate drop is a fold of two copies of one
work that were decided alike into one decision
by [[sessions reconcile]] (\cref{sec:session-copies}): a decided
copy the file holds under a tombstoned id and the session no longer
holds.  Only those are allowed for; a tombstone of an id the file does
not hold explains no drop.  Any drop beyond them is logged as a warning that names the
session, the two counts and the [[.bak]] that still holds the previous
version.  We warn rather than refuse: refusing would also throw away this
process's own work, and the [[.bak]] makes the loss recoverable.

<<review session functions>>=
def count_decided(decisions: list[ReviewDecision]) -> int:
    """Return how many of `decisions` are kept or discarded."""
    return sum(1 for d in decisions if d.is_decided)


def warn_if_decisions_dropped(
    session: ReviewSession, on_disk: ReviewSession | None, backup: Path
) -> None:
    """Warn when saving `session` would leave fewer decided papers than
    `on_disk` has, beyond the ones this process reset to pending."""
    if on_disk is None:
        return
    before = count_decided(on_disk.decisions)
    after = count_decided(session.decisions)
    base_states = session._baseline.decisions if session._baseline else {}
    reset_here = sum(
        1 for d in session.decisions
        if not d.is_decided
        and base_states.get(get_paper_id(d.paper), (DecisionStatus.PENDING,))[0]
        != DecisionStatus.PENDING
    )
    session_ids = {get_paper_id(d.paper) for d in session.decisions}
    folded_here = sum(
        1 for d in on_disk.decisions
        if d.is_decided and get_paper_id(d.paper) in session.folded
        and get_paper_id(d.paper) not in session_ids
    )
    if after + reset_here + folded_here < before:
        logger.warning(
            "Session %s: this save reduces the decided papers from %d to %d "
            "although no decision command reset them; the previous version "
            "is kept in %s",
            session.name or session.query, before, after, backup,
        )
<<warn if the save drops decisions>>=
warn_if_decisions_dropped(session, on_disk, backup_path(session_path))
