Let's verify it with real processes, as the issue describes the race:
both build the append from the same file and find the same new paper;
the second decides it and saves; then the first saves, without having
touched the paper.  The file must keep the second process's decision.
Separate processes also keep the paper registry, which one process
shares between its session objects, out of the test.

