The rule is used wherever a decision's providers attribute the paper to
a database: by [[decision_provider_names]] above, so a provider known
only from records without an outcome is not counted as searched on the
strength of a merged string, and by the audit rows' provider codes
([[collect_audit_rows]]), from which the caption's \enquote{Databases:}
sentence takes its rows part (\cref{sec:audit-databases}).  The stored
[[provider]] is not rewritten: it is what the search wrote, and the rule
can be revised without touching a session.  Displays of the stored
value ([[sessions show]], the TUI, the CSV export, the session JSON)
show it as stored.

The case of the issue: a merged search whose only paper came from
OpenAlex no longer names DBLP in the row, the caption or the report,
and DBLP is listed as queried without a recorded outcome; a paper with
a link to a DBLP search keeps DBLP; and a paper without evidence reads
as before.

