The summary says who decided before it says anything else about the
decisions (issue~\#163).  The kept, discarded and pending counts are
followed by one row per decision source ([[decision_source_items]],
\cref{sec:review-source}), so a review whose discards are mostly
unreviewed LLM output says so in the same place it gives the number of
discards.

When a machine took part in the review, the summary also reports how
many of its decisions the reviewer confirmed or changed, split by
direction; a session without such decisions omits those lines so the
table does not suggest a step that never happened.  A changed decision
is recognised by [[is_example]]: corrected decisions become training
examples for later LLM rounds, which is exactly the set we want to
count.  The LLM and the agent get separate rows because they are
separate procedures, and a reader judging how reliable the screening
was needs the agreement rate of each.  [[sessions export]] prints the
same rows, so [[machine_review_rows]] computes them once.

<<review report generation>>=
MACHINE_SOURCES = (
    ("LLM", ReviewSource.LLM_UNREVIEWED),
    ("Agent", ReviewSource.AGENT_UNREVIEWED),
)


def machine_review_rows(decisions) -> list[tuple[str, int]]:
    """Return `(label, count)` rows of confirmed and changed machine decisions.

    Rows appear per machine (LLM, agent) only when it decided something.
    """
    rows: list[tuple[str, int]] = []
    for name, unreviewed in MACHINE_SOURCES:
        reviewed = unreviewed.reviewed
        mine = [d for d in decisions if d.source in (unreviewed, reviewed)]
        if not mine:
            continue
        changed = [d for d in mine if d.source is reviewed and d.is_example]
        rows.extend([
            (f"{name} confirmed", sum(
                1 for d in mine if d.source is reviewed and not d.is_example
            )),
            (f"{name} changed", len(changed)),
            (f"{name} changed (kept->discarded)", sum(
                1 for d in changed if d.status == DecisionStatus.DISCARDED
            )),
            (f"{name} changed (discarded->kept)", sum(
                1 for d in changed if d.status == DecisionStatus.KEPT
            )),
        ])
    return rows
