A session's decisions are records, not works: the copies of one work
that the session could not fold (\cref{sec:session-copies}) are
separate decisions, so the total above can count one work twice.  The
audit table counts works ([[audit_work_key]], \cref{sec:audit-table}),
and a report that gives a different total for the same session invites
the question which one is right.  So the summary also states the number
of unique works, taken from the audit table's own rows, and, when there
are any, the copies left for the user: foldable (with the command
that folds them), conflicting, decided alike but not merged, and
possible copies not reconciled
(\cref{sec:session-copies}); [[sessions show]] lists them.

<<review report generation>>=
def report_work_items(session: ReviewSession) -> list[str]:
    """Report summary items for the works behind the session's records."""
    works = len(collect_audit_rows(
        session, theme_names={}, strings=AUDIT_STRINGS["en"]
    ))
    items = [f"\\item[Unique works] {works}"]
    for label, count, hint in (
        ("Foldable copies", len(foldable_copies(session)),
         ", see \\texttt{scholar sessions reconcile}"),
        ("Conflicting copies", len(conflicting_copies(session)), ""),
        ("Copies decided alike, not merged", len(alike_copies(session)), ""),
        ("Possible copies, not reconciled", len(possible_copies(session)),
         ""),
    ):
        if count:
            items.append(f"\\item[{label}] {count}{hint}")
    return items
@

