Records from before outcomes were kept (\cref{sec:unrecorded-outcome})
must not make a database count as searched.  The case comes from a real
session (\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholarcli/issues/188}): four
DBLP searches recorded in October 2026, without hits or error, while
DBLP served only its anti-bot page and no paper came from it; since the
sentence named databases from records, DBLP appeared among those
searched.  We check that such a database is listed apart, in both
languages, that a database the rows show is named as before, that one
answered query is enough to name it, and that the table's caption does
the same for the session.

